        "header": "1Introduction",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.02497/2611.02497v1/images/main_fig/robocolosseum-figure-1-v10.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:RoboColosseum overview.RoboColosseum connects distributed evaluation sites through shared robot interfaces, policy-serving infrastructure, and two complementary evaluation tracks.\nIn theFine-tune Track, policies receive the same 100 demonstrations per task and are evaluated on predefined tasks using common success and progress criteria.\nIn theOpen Track, policies are evaluated without additional task-specific adaptation through blinded, pairwise comparisons under matched local conditions, while tasks and environments vary across comparisons. The results shown for both tracks are based on evaluations we conducted from 17 September to 28 October 2026. The project spans SO-101, Franka in the DROID configuration, Bimanual-YAM, and Unitree G1, with participation determined by track and model compatibility.\nThe lower panels illustrate track-specific evaluation outputs and examples of physical evaluation settings.\nThe global network depicts the broader project vision; the scope of completed experiments is reported separately.",
                "position": 396
            }
        ]
    },
